From 26be3f0c6bc485a9777c5111c5a492444535dbc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saironcb <saironbusatto@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:35:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 44/44] feat: arena ML policy picks actions live, hot-reloads
 weights, champion/challenger

The ArenaMlMultiplier rescaled relevance after the queue had already chosen,
so it never changed which action ran. Instead, on a Playerbots.ArenaMlControl
share of ticks the net samples one of the combat actions the rules queued
(never emergencies or rule-owned movement/targeting) and lifts it to the top.

- Weight files and team lists are re-read every 10 s (no restart for a new
  policy); a second policy (ArenaMlChallengerFile/Teams) plays beside the
  champion for live A/B against the rules.
- Decision log v3 adds who decided (rules or net, with the net's probability)
  and the bot's running arena damage/healing/killing blows, so the live
  trainer can grade every decision.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vn4vD1fiBmsMGCCvsiqU7z
